Reaction Wheel Attitude Control
- Backstepping

  {
    "system_name": "Reaction Wheel Attitude Control",
    "states": ["x1", "x2", "x3"],
    "state_meanings": [
      "body attitude angle (rad)",
      "body angular rate (rad/s)",
      "motor current (A)"
    ],
    "inputs": ["u"],
    "outputs": ["x1"],
    "state_equations": [
      "x2",
      "-0.0016*x3",
      "-20*x3 + 10*u"
    ],
    "parameters": {},
    "system_type": "SISO",
    "assumptions": [
    ]
  }

intial: 0.05, 0, 0
refrence: The satellite should slew to point along a target line of sight that slowly sweeps back and forth by about 3 degrees at roughly 0.05 rad/s.
uncertanty: Delta(x) = [0, -8*tanh(5*x2), 0] on x2 (small unmodeled friction coupling from the wheel bearing into the body)
disturbance: solar radiation pressure and gravity-gradient torques slowly vary over the orbit; nobody has an exact formula for them, but the controller must still reject them.

===================================================

Quadrotor Altitude Channel
- Backstepping

  {
    "system_name": "Quadrotor Altitude Channel",
    "states": ["x1", "x2", "x3"],
    "state_meanings": [
      "altitude (m)",
      "vertical velocity (m/s)",
      "delivered thrust-per-unit-mass (m/s^2)"
    ],
    "inputs": ["u"],
    "outputs": ["x1"],
    "state_equations": [
      "x2",
      "x3 - 9.81 - 0.15*x2*Abs(x2)",
      "-8.333*x3 + 8.333*u"
    ],
    "parameters": {},
    "system_type": "SISO",
    "assumptions": [
    ]
  }

intial: 0, 0, 9.81
refrence: The quadrotor should climb to and then hover around 8 m altitude, gently bobbing about 0.5 m up and down once every about 4 seconds.
uncertanty: Delta(x) = 0.08*exp(-4*x1) - 0.04*x2 on x2 (ground effect boosting thrust near the ground, and the nominal drag coefficient being only a rough guess)
disturbance: eta, a slowly time-varying push from turbulent air near the flight arena, on x2; nobody has measured or modeled it, but it must still be accounted for.

===================================================

Twin-Rotor Pitch/Yaw Rig
- SMC

  {
    "system_name": "Twin-Rotor Pitch/Yaw Rig",
    "states": ["x1", "x2", "x3", "x4"],
    "state_meanings": [
      "pitch angle (rad)",
      "pitch angular rate (rad/s)",
      "yaw angle (rad)",
      "yaw angular rate (rad/s)"
    ],
    "inputs": ["u1", "u2"],
    "outputs": ["x1", "x3"],
    "state_equations": [
      "x2",
      "-2*sin(x1) - 0.5*x2 + 3*u1 + 0.8*u2",
      "x4",
      "-0.3*x4 + 0.6*u2 + 0.4*x2*x4"
    ],
    "parameters": {},
    "system_type": "MIMO",
    "assumptions": [
    ]
  }

intial: 0.1, 0, -0.05, 0
refrence: It should track y1_ref = 0.2*sin(t) (pitch oscillation) while yawing to and holding y2_ref = 0.3 (a fixed heading, step).
uncertanty: Delta(x) = [0, -0.15*tanh(4*x2), 0, 0.1*sin(x1)] on x2 and x4 (blade-flapping nonlinear damping on pitch, and reduced tail-rotor authority from main-rotor downwash as a function of pitch angle)
disturbance: mechanical vibration from slight motor imbalance on both axes; nobody has characterized it, but the controller must still reject it.

===================================================

Electro-Hydraulic Position Servo
- Backstepping

  {
    "system_name": "Electro-Hydraulic Position Servo",
    "states": ["x1", "x2", "x3"],
    "state_meanings": [
      "rod position from mid-stroke, positive extending (m)",
      "rod velocity (m/s)",
      "load pressure across the piston, as equivalent acceleration (m/s^2)"
    ],
    "inputs": ["u"],
    "outputs": ["x1"],
    "state_equations": [
      "x2",
      "x3 - 3.2*x2",
      "-180*x2 - 14*x3 + 260*u"
    ],
    "parameters": {},
    "system_type": "SISO",
    "assumptions": [
    ]
  }

intial: -0.008, 0, 0
refrence: It should hold a position 25 mm above mid-stroke while superimposing a gentle 6 mm oscillation at 1.5 rad/s.
uncertanty: Delta(x) = -0.9*tanh(25*x2) on x2 (friction from the rod seals, characterised on the bench)
disturbance: the machine presses a workpiece against the rod during the stroke, and the reaction force changes with every part; nobody has a formula for it, but the controller must still reject it.

===================================================

Flexible-Joint Robot Arm
- Backstepping

  {
    "system_name": "Flexible-Joint Robot Arm",
    "states": ["x1", "x2", "x3", "x4"],
    "state_meanings": [
      "link angle (rad)",
      "link angular rate (rad/s)",
      "motor angle (rad)",
      "motor angular rate (rad/s)"
    ],
    "inputs": ["u"],
    "outputs": ["x1"],
    "state_equations": [
      "x2",
      "-9.8*sin(x1) - 40*(x1 - x3)",
      "x4",
      "1000*(x1 - x3) + 50*u"
    ],
    "parameters": {},
    "system_type": "SISO",
    "assumptions": [
    ]
  }

intial: 0.3, 0, 0.3, 0
refrence: It should track y_ref = 0.4*sin(0.5*t).
uncertanty: Delta(x) = -0.6*tanh(8*x2) on x2 (Coulomb and viscous friction at the link pivot, characterised on the bench)
disturbance: an unmeasured payload/contact torque at the link (e.g. picking up an object of unknown mass, or brushing against the environment); nobody has a formula for it, but the controller must still reject it.
